    "title": "Nominalization -음",
    "title_ko": "명사화 -음",
    "focus_axis": "grammar"
  },
  "context": {
    "explanation_en": "« -음/-ㅁ » turns a verb into a noun, often used for facts or completed states. For example, « 그가 옳음을 알았어요 » (I realized that he was right).",
    "explanation_ko": "'-음/-ㅁ'은 동사를 명사로 바꾸며 흔히 사실이나 완료된 상태에 사용됩니다. 예: '그가 옳음을 알았어요'.",
    "key_expressions": [
      {
        "en": "I realized that he was right.",
        "ko": "그가 옳음을 알았어요."
      },
      {
        "en": "I'm sure that this is true.",
        "ko": "이것이 사실임을 확신해요."
      },
      {
        "an": "x",
        "en": "I regret not having tried.",
        "ko": "시도하지 않았음을 후회해요."
      }
    ]
  },
